about over‑interpretation in Aegean iconography.\n\nWhile Hudler does not re‑describe the ring’s discovery, she confirms its role as a key case study in debates over how to read Minoan and Mycenaean religious 
imagery, thus contributing to the **historical‑cultural context** of the Ring of Nestor as an object central to discussions of Minoan afterlife beliefs and epiphany scenes."
