 • A. G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the Quest for Authenticity,” in F. Blakolmer (ed.), Current Approaches and New Perspectives in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18, 2020, pp. 223–252. [2]                
 • The article “SOME OBSERVATIONS ON THE ICONOGRAPHY OF THE ‘RING OF NESTOR’” discusses the ring’s imagery and the debate over Aegean forgeries, stressing that iconography remains a crucial tool for assessing  
   authenticity when technical analyses are inconclusive. [3]                                                                                                                                                     
 • The study emphasises the presence of incurved altars in the scene depicted on the ‘Ring of Nestor’ and argues that this iconographic element supports the ring’s authenticity when compared with parallels on  
